1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,458
You grew up in Douala. Today, you live in Paris.

2
00:00:04,088 --> 00:00:08,288
One Saturday, you walk into an Afro shop. You're looking for njangsang.

3
00:00:08,823 --> 00:00:13,340
The seller has no idea. And yet, the product may be right there, on the shelf.

4
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:17,146
He grew up in Abidjan. Back home, it's called akpi.

5
00:00:17,709 --> 00:00:22,010
Same product. Two names. And no reliable list to connect them.

6
00:00:22,407 --> 00:00:24,474
That's why AfroAtlas exists.

7
00:00:25,061 --> 00:00:31,656
You type the name from home... and AfroAtlas shows you its other names, country by country, language by language.

8
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:35,271
Every name is linked to its source. Nothing is made up.

9
00:00:35,845 --> 00:00:39,976
Choose the seller's country, and show him the card: the name he knows.

10
00:00:40,664 --> 00:00:46,887
Soumbala in Mali, nététou in Senegal. Foléré in Cameroon, bissap-feuille in Senegal.

11
00:00:47,362 --> 00:00:53,610
Today: ninety-five records, one thousand thirty-five names, one hundred nineteen sources, thirteen countries.

12
00:00:54,152 --> 00:00:59,298
One product, many names. Find yours on AfroAtlas. Subscribe.
